# Vite UI build-time defaults.
#
# Committed to git, and compiled into the ONE bundle every hub is served
# from — so nothing here may belong to a particular hub. Until 2026-09-24
# this file held Floyd's tagline, intro text, page title, banner and
# governing body, and every hub without its own settings row showed them
# (Utopia opened with "This is where Floyd County residents…"). Those are
# Floyd's data now: config/hubs/floyd/settings.json, seeded into its
# hub_settings rows by scripts/seed-hub-settings.ts.
#
# What is left is used only by index.html's %VITE_VAR% substitution — the
# title and share card a crawler sees on "/" before JavaScript runs — and
# must read true for any hub. The running page replaces all of it from
# /api/hub-config at boot. A single-hub self-host may still override any
# VITE_HUB_* in its Vercel project's environment; that is a deployment
# choice, not something this file may assume.
#
# DO NOT put secrets in this file — it ships in the bundle.

VITE_HUB_PAGE_TITLE=Civic Hub
VITE_HUB_DESCRIPTION=Vote on local issues, raise what matters, and see where your community stands.
VITE_HUB_BANNER_URL=
VITE_HUB_BANNER_ALT=
